From: Fractal Microsystems <opensource@fractalmicro.org>
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: omit Probe Request IEs for passive scans

A scan without SSIDs is passive and emits no Probe Request frames.
Supplicant-generated Extended Capabilities still reach scan_common in this
case. Passing them as NL80211_ATTR_IE unnecessarily rejects a passive scan
on a wiphy with max_scan_ie_len=0, before its scan callback is invoked.

Only attach Probe Request IEs when probes were requested. Active scans retain
their supplied IEs and the kernel's length validation; this does not silently
discard an active scan's requested capabilities or inflate the driver limit.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Fractal Microsystems <opensource@fractalmicro.org>

diff --git a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_scan.c
@@ -221,7 +221,8 @@ nl80211_scan_common(struct i802_bss *bss, u8 cmd,
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "nl80211: Passive scan requested");
 	}
 
-	if (params->extra_ies) {
+	/* Passive scans have no Probe Requests to carry these IEs. */
+	if (params->extra_ies && params->num_ssids) {
 		wpa_hexdump(MSG_MSGDUMP, "nl80211: Scan extra IEs",
 			    params->extra_ies, params->extra_ies_len);
 		if (nla_put(msg, NL80211_ATTR_IE, params->extra_ies_len,
